==English==
{{was wotd|2021|November|29}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|shore|t=to provide with support}} + {{m|en|up}}. {{m|en||Shore}} is derived from Late {{inh|en|enm|shoren|t=to prop, to support}}{{nb...|schore, ssore|otherforms=1}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=shōren|pos=''v.''(1)|noformat=1|id=MED40045}}</ref><ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|entry=shore|pos=''v.''{{sup|1}}|noformat=1|id=178556|date=March 2021|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|alt=shore{{sup|2}}|pos=v}}</ref> from {{m|enm|shore|t=a prop, a support}}{{nb...|schore, score|otherforms=1}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=shōre|pos=''n.''(3)|noformat=1|id=MED40043}}</ref> + {{m|enm|-en|pos={{glossary|suffix}} forming the {{glossary|infinitive}} form of {{glossary|verb}}s}};<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=-en|pos=''suf.''(3)|noformat=1|id=MED13518}}</ref> while {{m|enm||shore|pos=noun}} is from {{der|en|dum|schore}}, {{m|dum|schare|t=a prop, a stay}} (modern {{cog|nl|schoor}}), and {{der|en|gml|schōre}}, {{m|gml|schāre|t=a prop, a stay; barrier; stockade}} (compare {{cog|non|skorða|t=a prop, a stay}} ({{cog|no|skor}}, {{m|no|skorda}})); further etymology unknown.<ref>{{R:OED Online|entry=shore|pos=''n.''{{sup|3}}|noformat=1|id=178551|date=March 2021|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|alt=shore{{sup|2}}|pos=n}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ʃɔːˈɹ‿ʌp/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ʃɔˈɹ‿ʌp/|a=GA,CA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ʃoːˈɹ‿ɐp/|a=AU,NZ}}
** {{audio|en|En-au-shore up.ogg|a=Queensland}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|often|figuratively}} To [[reinforce]] or [[strengthen]] (something [[at risk]] of [[failure]]).
#: {{synonyms|en|q1=rare|embolster|prop up|underfoot|undergird|underpin|underprop|underset}}
#: {{ux|en|They [[hasten|hastened]] outside between storms to '''shore up''' the damaged fence.}}
#: {{ux|en|He needed something bold and dramatic to '''shore up''' his failing [[candidacy]].}}
#: {{ux|en|I '''shored up''' a [[geranium]] with earth after it had flopped over.}}
#* {{RQ:Twain American Claimant|chapter=XXII|pages=233–234|pageref=234|passage=This answer fell just at the right time and just in the right place, to save the poor unstable young man from changing his political complexion once more. He had been on the point of beginning to totter again, but this prop '''shored''' him '''up''' and kept him from floundering back into democracy and re-renouncing aristocracy.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Jamie Lillywhite|title=[[w:Tottenham Hotspur F.C.|Tottenham]] 1 – 0 [[w:FC Rubin Kazan|Rubin Kazan]]|work=w:BBC Sport|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210830181549/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/europe/15285221.stm|archivedate=30 August 2021|date=20 October 2011|passage=[[w:Harry Redknapp|[Harry] Redknapp]] was determined to secure victory and sent on {{w|Younes Kaboul}} and star playmaker [[w:Luka Modrić|Luka Modric]] to '''shore''' things '''up'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|author=Marcus Chown|title=Infinity in the Palm of Your Hand{{...|: Fifty Wonders That Reveal an Extraordinary Universe}}|publisher=Michael O'Mara Books|isbn=9781782439509|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=Yj5sDwAAQBAJ&pg=PT210&dq=%22hand+waving%22&hl=&cd=35&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22hand%20waving%22&f=false|text=However, in 1998, the Argentinean-American physicist Juan Maldacena published a paper that '''shored up''' the idea that we live in a ‘holographic universe’ and set the world of physics alight.}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|url=https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2022/oct/19/suella-braverman-departs-as-uk-home-secretary-liz-truss|title=Suella Braverman forced to resign as UK home secretary|date=2022-10-19|passage=[Liz Truss] had cleared her diary and called off a planned visit amid desperate attempts to '''shore up''' her premiership, before speaking to Braverman at a meeting in the House of Commons, sources said.}}
#* {{RQ:NYT|title=Trump Promises Farmers $12 Billion to Blunt Fallout From His Trade War|date=Dec. 8, 2025|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/12/08/us/politics/trump-farmers-aid-bailout.html|passage=President Trump rolled out a $12 billion bailout for struggling farmers on Monday as he looks to '''shore up''' the finances of some of his most loyal supporters whose financial fortunes have been hurt by his trade war.}}

